From f352fe07e442574030eeb5359986a9b2aa5c2704 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 18:08:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Model onboarding: remove self-selects, enforce age 18+ &
 gov ID, fix Rekognition linkage
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Top-tier pass on model onboarding per demo requirements.

Removed ALL self-select attribute inputs:
- Deleted the "Confirm your look" dropdowns and the "Quick features
  (self-selected)" hair length/color/texture selects in the Modeling-path step.
- Replaced with a read-only "AI vision analysis" step: attributes are detected
  from photos via Rekognition + the Modeled hair/beauty engine (shows detected
  values when present, otherwise an "analyzing" state).

Age verification (18+): DOB now required in Basic Info and enforced both on
step advance and at submit (isAdult/ageFromBirthday helpers). Under-18 or
missing DOB cannot proceed. ageRange still derived for matching.

Gov ID verification: now required to submit (verified/manual_review) unless
explicitly bypassed for dev/test (allowOnboardingVerificationBypass) — grouped
with email/phone verification enforcement.

Fixed the Rekognition linkage bug (why auto-attributes never populated):
- Photos are stored under the Cognito identity-pool id, but ModelProfile is
  keyed by Cognito sub, so photo-analysis could never find the profile.
- Added ModelProfile.storageIdentityId; onboarding now (a) creates a profile
  draft BEFORE photo upload so the S3 trigger has a target, and (b) sets
  storageIdentityId on the profile.
- photo-analysis Lambda now matches a profile by userId (sub) OR
  storageIdentityId, so uploads link correctly.

NOTE: the Rekognition/linkage changes require an Amplify deploy + Bedrock model
access to take effect and have not been runtime-tested from this environment.

Verified here: backend tsc clean, Vite build passes, 42/42 matching tests green.

