+# Model Onboarding — DEMO TODAY Runbook
+
+**Date:** 2026-06-07
+**Read this first.** It separates what is **done in code** from what **only you can do in AWS** (I have no access to your AWS account from my environment).
+
+---
+
+## What changed (code — done & verified to build)
+
+1. **No more self-selects.** Removed every hair/skin/eye dropdown — both the "Confirm your look" step and the hidden "Quick features (self-selected)" selects in the Modeling-path step. Replaced with a read-only **"AI vision analysis"** step.
+2. **Age 18+ verification.** DOB is required and **18+ is enforced** at step advance and at submit. Under-18 cannot continue. (Client-side — works immediately, no backend.)
+3. **Gov ID required.** Submission now requires ID verification (verified/manual_review) unless dev-bypassed.
+4. **Rekognition linkage fixed.** Root cause found: photos are stored under the Cognito **identity id**, but profiles are keyed by Cognito **sub** — so analysis never matched. Now: a profile **draft is created before photo upload**, `storageIdentityId` is stored, and the Lambda matches on **sub OR storageIdentityId**.
+5. **Photo upload hardened.** Identity resolved at upload time with refresh fallback (no more "Preparing secure upload…" dead-end).
+
+**Verified in my environment:** backend `tsc` clean · Vite build passes · 42/42 matching tests green.
+
+---
+
+## ⚠️ The honest part: what must happen in YOUR AWS for the demo to actually work
+
+I cannot deploy or configure AWS from here. These are required and only take ~20–30 min:
+
+### A. Deploy the backend (required for everything server-side)
+```bash
+# in your Cursor clone, after applying the patches
+npx ampx sandbox        # or: npx ampx pipeline-deploy --branch main --app-id <id>
+```
+This creates the new `ModelProfile` columns (`storageIdentityId`, etc.) and ships the photo-analysis Lambda fix.
+
+### B. Email verification — why it "doesn't work"
+- The **code is correct** (standard Cognito attribute verification). With Amplify Gen 2 `loginWith: { email: true }`, **Cognito verifies email at sign-up** using its default email sender — this should work once deployed.
+- If emails aren't arriving: Cognito default email has a low daily cap. For reliable sending, verify an **SES** identity and set `AMPLIFY_SES_FROM_EMAIL` (your `auth/resource.ts` already supports this).
+
+### C. SMS verification — the hard one
+- Cognito SMS needs **Amazon SNS** with an **origination number / spending limit**, and in the SNS **sandbox** every destination number must be pre-verified. Same-day SMS to arbitrary numbers usually isn't possible without leaving the sandbox (AWS approval).
+- **Demo recommendation:** keep phone as "verify **or skip**" (already implemented) and demo **email + gov ID + age** as the verification story. Pursue SNS production access separately.
+
+### D. Rekognition + Bedrock (for the AI vision analysis)
+- **Bedrock → Model access** (us-east-1): enable **Claude 3.5 Sonnet + Haiku**.
+- The `photo-analysis` IAM (Rekognition + Bedrock) was fixed in an earlier patch — make sure that patch is applied + deployed.
+- After deploy, uploaded photos trigger analysis → attributes attach to the profile (via the linkage fix) → show in admin and feed matching.
+
+### E. Cognito Admin group (to see the admin side)
+- Cognito → your User Pool → Groups → **Admin** → add your user.
+
+---
+
+## Demo-day env flags (`.env.local`, then restart `npm run dev`)
+
+**Option 1 — Full real verification (best story, needs A–E above):**
+```env
+VITE_USE_MOCK_DATA=false
+VITE_FULL_APP_ACCESS=true
+VITE_BYPASS_ONBOARDING_VERIFICATION=false   # require email + ID
+VITE_SKIP_IDENTITY_VERIFICATION=false        # require gov ID
+```
+
+**Option 2 — Safe fallback if SMS/Rekognition aren't ready:**
+```env
+VITE_USE_MOCK_DATA=false
+VITE_FULL_APP_ACCESS=true
+VITE_BYPASS_ONBOARDING_VERIFICATION=true    # skip email/SMS/ID gates for the walkthrough
+```
+*Age 18+ is still enforced in Option 2 (it's client-side and always on).*
+
+---
+
+## The flow you'll demo (11 steps)
+
+```
+Basic Info (DOB → 18+ gate) → Modeling path → Service prefs → Availability
+→ Photos (3+, upload to S3) → AI vision analysis (Rekognition, read-only)
+→ Data Privacy & Terms → Review → Email verify → Phone verify (or skip)
+→ Gov ID verify (ID + selfie, Rekognition face match) → Submit
+→ /admin/onboarding (pending) → Approve → active
+```
+
+---
+
+## Straight talk
+- **Works the moment you deploy + flag:** no self-selects, age 18+, the full guided flow, photo upload, gov-ID upload UI, admin capture.
+- **Needs the AWS config above to be "live":** email delivery (SES), SMS (SNS — hardest), Rekognition auto-attributes + ID face-match (deploy + Bedrock access).
+- **Not runtime-tested by me:** the Rekognition linkage + draft-create path (no AWS access here). Please smoke-test after deploy: onboard a model → check the `ModelProfile` row gets `autoTaggedAttributes` after photo analysis.
+
+If anything errors during your deploy/smoke test, paste the error and I'll fix it fast.
